{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463406",
      "title": "Introducing Components",
      "lectureOrder": 73,
      "videoOrder": 65,
      "sourceHash": "5bcf1357f08afc9f1767496084a94f71c45492ab194e71c03e6bf10a007597d0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "Components are a great,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 7.45,
          "en": "if you have certain pieces of HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.45,
          "end": 10.26,
          "en": "Certain HTML blocks like here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.26,
          "end": 13.84,
          "en": "which you reuse in different parts of your page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.84,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "like here, where we create multiple list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 20.25,
          "en": "Where you then have a certain functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.25,
          "end": 23.47,
          "en": "that should be enclosed in that HTML block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.47,
          "end": 27.25,
          "en": "And that should be specific to this HTML block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.25,
          "end": 28.72,
          "en": "Components can also be great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.72,
          "end": 30.72,
          "en": "to splitting your big application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.72,
          "end": 32.81,
          "en": "into multiple smaller chunks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.81,
          "end": 35.9,
          "en": "but that's something we'll explore later automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.9,
          "end": 39.03,
          "en": "once we work more and more with components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.03,
          "end": 42.54,
          "en": "So, since components seem to be very helpful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.54,
          "end": 44.55,
          "en": "how can we create such a component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.55,
          "end": 46.2,
          "en": "How does it work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.2,
          "end": 50.51,
          "en": "A component is the official feature Vue.js knows,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.51,
          "end": 53.59,
          "en": "and we can create one on an app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.59,
          "end": 57.15,
          "en": "So on an app we create it with create app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.15,
          "end": 59.84,
          "en": "by using that app which in my case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.84,
          "end": 62.4,
          "en": "is stored in that app constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 65.75,
          "en": "and calling the component method on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.75,
          "end": 70.503,
          "en": "This tells Vue that we want to create a new component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.35,
          "end": 74.87,
          "en": "Now this component method needs two things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.87,
          "end": 77.88,
          "en": "The first thing is an identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.88,
          "end": 80.05,
          "en": "because a component and that's important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.05,
          "end": 81.42,
          "en": "you have to memorize this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.42,
          "end": 86.42,
          "en": "A component is basically like a custom HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 90.42,
          "en": "So here you define your own HTML tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.31,
          "end": 92.65,
          "en": "and that could for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.65,
          "end": 96.47999999999999,
          "en": "be user dash contact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.43,
          "end": 100.59,
          "en": "or friend dash contact, something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.59,
          "end": 105.34,
          "en": "You should always use an identifier that contains a dash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.34,
          "end": 107.89,
          "en": "So you should always have component names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.89,
          "end": 111.50999999999999,
          "en": "custom HTML tags therefor which contained a dash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.50999999999999,
          "end": 114.25999999999999,
          "en": "so which are made up of two words.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.25999999999999,
          "end": 115.88,
          "en": "The reason for that is simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.88,
          "end": 118.69,
          "en": "this avoids that you potentially clash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.69,
          "end": 122.17,
          "en": "with official built in HTML elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.17,
          "end": 125.56,
          "en": "For example, if it would name my component h2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.56,
          "end": 128.78,
          "en": "well, there already is h2 element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.78,
          "end": 131.11,
          "en": "and that would therefore clash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.11,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "Therefore, a simple rule is that you should use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 138.82999999999998,
          "en": "multi word component names, so custom HTML tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.41,
          "end": 142.5,
          "en": "because all built in HTML elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.5,
          "end": 144.663,
          "en": "are a single word elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.56,
          "end": 149.29,
          "en": "So that's now my own HTML element name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.29,
          "end": 152.25,
          "en": "which we will later be able to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.25,
          "end": 156.19,
          "en": "This is the identifier of our components so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.19,
          "end": 160.05,
          "en": "The second argument you pass to this component method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.05,
          "end": 165.05,
          "en": "is a conflict object just as you pass it to create app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.27,
          "end": 167.86,
          "en": "because, and that's another important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.86,
          "end": 170.19,
          "en": "piece of information to keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.19,
          "end": 174.32,
          "en": "A Vue component is essentially just another Vue app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.32,
          "end": 177.483,
          "en": "just an app that belongs to another app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.42000000000002,
          "end": 182.71,
          "en": "So this which we're creating here is a new Vue app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.71,
          "end": 184.77,
          "en": "but, and that's the important thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.77,
          "end": 188.84,
          "en": "an app which will be connected to our main app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.84,
          "end": 192.84,
          "en": "So components are like mini apps you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.84,
          "end": 194.54,
          "en": "So therefore they can also have data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.54,
          "end": 197.44,
          "en": "they can have methods and therefore a here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 197.44,
          "end": 200.96,
          "en": "our component can have its own data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.96,
          "end": 205.96,
          "en": "where we, for example, have a detailsAreVisible property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.88,
          "end": 209.453,
          "en": "which initially is false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.55,
          "end": 213.06,
          "en": "We can also add methods to our component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.06,
          "end": 216.25,
          "en": "and add our toggle details method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.25,
          "end": 219.303,
          "en": "here to the methods of my own component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.52,
          "end": 224.2,
          "en": "So that we then toggle this component specific data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.2,
          "end": 226.603,
          "en": "with this component specific method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 227.7,
          "end": 230.74,
          "en": "And we can remove methods from the main app now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 230.74,
          "end": 233.06,
          "en": "and also get rid of details are visible there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.06,
          "end": 234.7,
          "en": "We could also keep it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.7,
          "end": 237.4,
          "en": "we wouldn't have a clash because this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.4,
          "end": 239.47,
          "en": "is essentially encapsulated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.47,
          "end": 242.86,
          "en": "It does not communicate with the parent app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.86,
          "end": 244.7,
          "en": "so with the app it belongs to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.7,
          "end": 246.7,
          "en": "but we can still remove this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.7,
          "end": 249.933,
          "en": "because we don't need it in the main app anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.77,
          "end": 255.24,
          "en": "So now we got our component, friend contact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.24,
          "end": 257.93,
          "en": "and how do we now use this component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.93,
          "end": 259.33299999999997,
          "en": "And how does it work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.22,
          "end": 263.55,
          "en": "Well, this component misses one important thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 263.55,
          "end": 264.96,
          "en": "before we can use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 264.96,
          "end": 268.05,
          "en": "And that's a template since this is a new app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.05,
          "end": 270.2,
          "en": "it needs its own template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 270.2,
          "end": 274.18,
          "en": "Our main app has a template, this whole section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.18,
          "end": 276.49,
          "en": "which we mounted the app to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.49,
          "end": 278.637,
          "en": "but our component now is a mini app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.637,
          "end": 281.27,
          "en": "and it needs its own template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 281.27,
          "end": 283.49,
          "en": "Now, here we don't mount this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 283.49,
          "end": 285.95,
          "en": "we don't call mount on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.95,
          "end": 289.023,
          "en": "so that's not how we will connect it to HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.86,
          "end": 292.2,
          "en": "Instead here for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 292.2,
          "end": 294.90999999999997,
          "en": "we'll add this template option,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 294.90999999999997,
          "end": 297.40999999999997,
          "en": "which I also showed in the deep dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 297.40999999999997,
          "end": 299.403,
          "en": "in the behind the scenes module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 300.32,
          "end": 301.75,
          "en": "In case you skipped that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 301.75,
          "end": 303.43,
          "en": "yes there is a template option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 303.43,
          "end": 307.66,
          "en": "which you can add to your view apps also to the main app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 307.66,
          "end": 310.31,
          "en": "to define the template of that app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 310.31,
          "end": 313.67,
          "en": "So to define the HTML code of that app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 313.67,
          "end": 316.173,
          "en": "and you need to do that for this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 317.71,
          "end": 320.14,
          "en": "Now I will already say that later in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 320.14,
          "end": 321.57,
          "en": "in the next modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 321.57,
          "end": 324.32,
          "en": "we will learn about a much nicer way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 324.32,
          "end": 326.12,
          "en": "of defining those templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 326.12,
          "end": 330.03,
          "en": "But for the moment, I'll just create a multiline string here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 330.03,
          "end": 331.5,
          "en": "with backticks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 331.5,
          "end": 335.02,
          "en": "So these are not single quotes, these are backticks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 335.02,
          "end": 337.75,
          "en": "which is a different character on the keyboard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 337.75,
          "end": 341.12,
          "en": "And I will now grab this list item here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 341.12,
          "end": 346.12,
          "en": "so these entire code and cut it from my HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 347,
          "end": 352,
          "en": "and instead added here in this backticked string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 352.06,
          "end": 355.06,
          "en": "And I'm using backticks because they allow me to write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 355.06,
          "end": 356.97,
          "en": "a multiline string like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.97,
          "end": 359.75,
          "en": "But in the end, that's just a JavaScript string now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.75,
          "end": 362.463,
          "en": "With all those view features in it though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 363.55,
          "end": 368.16,
          "en": "now, I will remove that v4 code on the list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 368.16,
          "end": 370.44,
          "en": "and to make sure the interpolations work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 370.44,
          "end": 375.44,
          "en": "for the moment I will add a friend property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 375.49,
          "end": 377.49,
          "en": "to the data off that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 377.49,
          "end": 379.343,
          "en": "so not friends, but friend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 380.93,
          "end": 384.93,
          "en": "And I will just copy one friend which I defined here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 384.93,
          "end": 389.93,
          "en": "Let's take manual and store him in this friend key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 391.23,
          "end": 392.74,
          "en": "This is just temporary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 392.74,
          "end": 395.18,
          "en": "we'll soon make it work with our list again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 395.18,
          "end": 397.92,
          "en": "but to get started, we'll just use friend like that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 399.17,
          "end": 400.55,
          "en": "And now if I save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 400.55,
          "end": 404,
          "en": "we can finally start using our own component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 404,
          "end": 407.35,
          "en": "and therefore our own HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 407.35,
          "end": 410.15,
          "en": "Because now we can go to index HTML",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 410.15,
          "end": 413.25,
          "en": "and instead of our main apps template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 413.25,
          "end": 417.81,
          "en": "we can now use friend contact as if it would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 417.81,
          "end": 420.363,
          "en": "an official HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 421.5,
          "end": 424.57,
          "en": "And it's not, I really want to emphasize it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 424.57,
          "end": 428.78,
          "en": "This is not an HTML element which the browser would know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 428.78,
          "end": 431.78,
          "en": "If you try to use that outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 431.78,
          "end": 435.58,
          "en": "of the Vue app controlled part, this will do nothing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 435.58,
          "end": 437.66,
          "en": "the browser will ignore it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 437.66,
          "end": 442.05,
          "en": "But inside of our main app Vue will understand this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 442.05,
          "end": 444.15,
          "en": "it will understand this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 444.15,
          "end": 448.02,
          "en": "because we registered this component to our main app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 448.02,
          "end": 449.6,
          "en": "with the component method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 449.6,
          "end": 452.4,
          "en": "by giving it that exact identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 452.4,
          "end": 456.623,
          "en": "which I'm now using as an HTML tag in my template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 457.95,
          "end": 459.28,
          "en": "And that's why we should use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 459.28,
          "end": 462.25,
          "en": "a non-default HTML tag name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 462.25,
          "end": 465.35,
          "en": "because if we would have named our component h2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 465.35,
          "end": 469.56,
          "en": "Vue would not recognize it as a custom component of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 469.56,
          "end": 473.12,
          "en": "But since we have such a name with a dash in it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 473.12,
          "end": 476.96,
          "en": "a two word name, which is this identifier we used here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 476.96,
          "end": 480.54,
          "en": "Vue detects that here in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 480.54,
          "end": 484.81,
          "en": "we wanna render this mini app with its template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 484.81,
          "end": 487.513,
          "en": "and all the dynamic pieces in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 488.76,
          "end": 491.113,
          "en": "So now if we save this again and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 492.03,
          "end": 494.46,
          "en": "we see Manual Lorenz on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 494.46,
          "end": 496.86,
          "en": "and we can click show details and hide details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 496.86,
          "end": 498.89,
          "en": "and this just works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 498.89,
          "end": 501.06,
          "en": "And now we can repeat that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 501.06,
          "end": 503.92,
          "en": "and simply add a number of component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 503.92,
          "end": 506.9,
          "en": "And if I reload, we have Manuel Lorenz twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 506.9,
          "end": 510.81,
          "en": "and the important thing is every Manual Lorenz,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 510.81,
          "end": 515.04,
          "en": "works, stand-alone, totally detached from the other one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 515.04,
          "end": 517.63,
          "en": "Now, of course we have the same data twice now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 517.63,
          "end": 519.58,
          "en": "that's something we're going to fix soon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 519.58,
          "end": 522.2,
          "en": "but this shows you how components allow you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 522.2,
          "end": 527.2,
          "en": "to easily replicate and encapsulated piece of HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 527.82,
          "end": 530.17,
          "en": "with, and that's the important part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 530.17,
          "end": 533.54,
          "en": "with attached data and logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 533.54,
          "end": 537.52,
          "en": "So components are reusable pieces of HTML",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 537.52,
          "end": 540.7,
          "en": "with connected data and logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 540.7,
          "end": 543.18,
          "en": "And that is very, very powerful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 543.18,
          "end": 545.6,
          "en": "especially as you will soon see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 545.6,
          "end": 549.17,
          "en": "how we can also reuse one and the same component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 549.17,
          "end": 553.63,
          "en": "with different data that we pass into the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 553.63,
          "end": 555.12,
          "en": "That will be the next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 555.12,
          "end": 559.09,
          "en": "which will then really make components a powerful tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 559.09,
          "end": 561.35,
          "en": "But you can hopefully already see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 561.35,
          "end": 565.09,
          "en": "how a component helps us encapsulate structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 565.09,
          "end": 570.09,
          "en": "content and logic into small reusable pieces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 570.42,
          "end": 573.73,
          "en": "And you can really add as many of these components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 573.73,
          "end": 576.35,
          "en": "here as you want, and they will all be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 576.35,
          "end": 578.83,
          "en": "and they all work, stand-alone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 578.83,
          "end": 581.62,
          "en": "So now we've got a bunch of Vue mini apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 581.62,
          "end": 583.76,
          "en": "in the same main app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 583.76,
          "end": 587.53,
          "en": "And these apps will then also be able to communicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 587.53,
          "end": 590.02,
          "en": "with each other to share information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 590.02,
          "end": 592.97,
          "en": "and hence we'll have the best of both roles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 592.97,
          "end": 596.74,
          "en": "Encapsulated, isolated pieces of code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 596.74,
          "end": 599.23,
          "en": "which also makes it easier to work on that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 599.23,
          "end": 601.34,
          "en": "in case you have bigger projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 601.34,
          "end": 602.92,
          "en": "And at the same time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 602.92,
          "end": 606.07,
          "en": "we can combine all those isolated pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 606.07,
          "end": 608.5,
          "en": "to build a bigger app from them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 608.5,
          "end": 610.42,
          "en": "Now that's our components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 610.42,
          "end": 612.55,
          "en": "and they will be super important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 612.55,
          "end": 613.55,
          "en": "and we're going to use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 613.55,
          "end": 615.14,
          "en": "throughout the rest of the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 615.14,
          "end": 616.64,
          "en": "But at the same time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 616.64,
          "end": 619.56,
          "en": "we're now already reaching a part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 619.56,
          "end": 624.56,
          "en": "where this setup we used thus far has certain limitations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 624.92,
          "end": 628.32,
          "en": "We'll have more and more code in the same file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 628.32,
          "end": 632.38,
          "en": "and writing templates like this in such a string form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 632.38,
          "end": 635.21,
          "en": "that will not be very nice to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 635.21,
          "end": 636.99,
          "en": "In addition we of course also need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 636.99,
          "end": 638.78,
          "en": "to learn more about components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 638.78,
          "end": 642.11,
          "en": "so that we can really make this component reusable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 642.11,
